Package: thunderbolt-net-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms (>= 3.0.10)
Description: Thunderbolt networking driver with RX path-MTU reconstruction (DKMS)
 Out-of-tree thunderbolt_net driver tracking upstream Linux, with a
 receive-side workaround for peers that send TCP aggregates without
 segment boundaries (macOS Thunderbolt Bridge with TSO): it validates the
 aggregate, attaches conservative GSO metadata bounded by the flow's
 learned path MTU, and keeps the aggregate intact so local delivery stays
 fast and forwarding segments only where the path requires it.
 .
 This package contains source, built by DKMS for the target kernel.
 A modprobe file in /usr/lib/modprobe.d enables the workaround and RX page
 recycling on the next module load; override it from /etc/modprobe.d.
 Installation does not request unloading or reloading an active network module.
